ear>1998</year>. Association of ezrin with intercellular adhesion molecule-1 and -2 (ICAM-1 and ICAM-2). Regulation by phosphatidylinositol 4, 5-bisphosphate. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>21893</fpage>&#x02013;21900.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9705328</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Helander, T.S., O. Carpen, O. Turunen, P.E. Kovanen, A. Vaheri, and T. Timonen. <year>1996</year>. ICAM-2 redistributed by ezrin as a target for killer cells. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>382</volume>:<fpage>265</fpage>&#x02013;268.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8717043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Hirao, M., N. Sato, T. Kondo, S. Yonemura, M. Monden, T. Sasaki, Y. Takai, and S. Tsukita. <year>1996</year>. Regulation mechanism of ERM (ezrin/radixin/moesin) protein/plasma membrane association: possible involvement of phosphatidylinositol turnover and Rho-dependent signaling pathway. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>135</volume>:<fpage>37</fpage>&#x02013;51.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8858161</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Honda, A., M. Nogami, T. Yokozeki, M. Yamazaki, H. Nakamura, H. Watanabe, K. Kawamoto, K. Nakayama, A.J. Morris, M.A. Frohman, and Y. Kanaho. <year>1999</year>. Phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 5-kinase alpha is a downstream effector of the small G protein ARF6 in membrane ruffle formation. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>99</volume>:<fpage>521</fpage>&#x02013;532.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10589680</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Hyman, T., M. Shmuel, and Y. Altschuler. <year>2006</year>. Actin is required for endocytosis at the apical surface of Madin-Darby canine kidney cells where ARF6 and clathrin regulate the actin cytoskeleton. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>427</fpage>&#x02013;437.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16251360</pub-id></c